# The runner image builds with the REPOSITORY ROOT as its context (src/Enlist.Runner/Dockerfile
# explains why), and without this file every byte of that root is handed to the engine on every
# build. Two consequences, one slow and one worse:
#
#   - bin/ and obj/ across every project, .git, and the demo's own state make the transfer far larger
#     than the handful of source files the Dockerfile actually copies;
#   - demo/sql-server/.env holds the SA password in clear text, and it left the working tree on every
#     build even though nothing ever copied it into a layer.
#
# Nothing here was ever IN the image. The point is that it stopped being sent.

**/bin/
**/obj/
.git/
.vs/
.demo/
.testplugins/
deploy/
**/.env
**/*.user
**/TestResults/
docs/
